# UI Rule: Home Page Is The Source Of Truth

When editing or creating pages, the frontend design must follow the `Home` page look first. Treat `Home` as the baseline for spacing, heading hierarchy, section rhythm, and card stacking.

## Required Layout Pattern

- Use page shell: `px-5 pt-14 pb-6` for top-level pages.
- Use section spacing like `mb-6`, `mt-6`, and container gaps like `space-y-6`/`space-y-7` to create clear separation between cards.
- Match `Home` heading hierarchy: pretitle/supporting line, then main title with `text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mt-1 font-display` when appropriate.
- Section labels should follow the `Home` pattern: `text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-widest mb-3`.
- Subtitles: `text-muted-foreground text-xs mt-0.5`.

## Required Card Pattern

- Prefer `.app-card` and `.app-card-interactive` for reusable surfaces.
- For custom blocks, match existing card style: `bg-card rounded-2xl border border-border/50`.
- Use `overflow-hidden` + `divide-y divide-border/30` for list rows inside cards.
- Keep rounded pills/tags with `rounded-full` and soft backgrounds like `bg-primary/10`.
- Do not add decorative background shapes (floating squares/circles/blobs) behind card content.
- Avoid icon background squares unless they communicate state; prefer clean standalone icons.
- Avoid square swatch blocks for visual-only accents; use subtle pills/lines/dots instead.
- Keep row text away from right borders by adding extra horizontal padding (`px-6`) and text-side right padding (`pr-3` or `pr-4`) when needed.
- Avoid solid accent-background heading blocks unless explicitly requested; prefer neutral heading cards with accent used in chips/borders only.

## Colors, Typography, and Tokens

- Use theme tokens (`text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-card`, `border-border`), not hardcoded random colors.
- The only strong brand accent is cyan (`#1FD0EF` / `primary`), used intentionally for highlights.
- Keep body text compact (`text-sm`, `text-xs`) and clear hierarchy via weight, not oversized text.

## Motion and Interaction

- Use subtle `framer-motion` enter animations (`y: -10`/`16`, short delays).
- Hover/press feedback should stay soft (`hover:bg-primary/20`, tiny scale, no dramatic effects).
- Preserve readable states: unread, active, selected via border/background contrast.

## Page Intent to Preserve

- `home`: greeting header, up-next block, stacked cards (`card-list`).
- `schedule`: day selector chips + detailed/compact event cards.
- `notifications`: stacked interactive cards with unread emphasis.
- `details`: large title, metadata cards, about/rating sections.

## Applying This to MediaKit and Logistics

- Keep current structure and restyle by reusing shared card patterns before adding new custom CSS.
- If a style repeats 3+ times, move it to `index.css` as a semantic class (same approach as existing `event-detail-*` helpers).
- Do not introduce a separate visual language for these pages; they must look native to the same app.
- Keep page headings exactly aligned with main page pattern (`text-2xl font-bold text-foreground font-display` + `text-muted-foreground text-xs mt-0.5`).
- In conflicts between page-specific styling and shared styling, prefer the `Home` visual language.
- Apply the same card treatment to all content groups in a page (not only the first block).
- Implement spacing/padding consistency with reusable CSS classes in `index.css` (for example section gap classes and row/content padding classes), not only inline utility classes.
- For visible UI refinements (padding, spacing, emphasis, icon/text distance), prefer editing reusable CSS classes in `index.css` first, then reference those classes in JSX.

## Example (Preferred)

```css
.logistics-section-card {
  background-color: hsl(var(--card));
  border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border) / 0.5);
  border-radius: 1rem;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```
